+## Delivery and remaining acceptance
+
+The local candidate is **`bmt-trajectory:3437a5e036e344a13941`**; [image receipt](evidence/trajectory-verification-2026-10-09/linux-image.json). It was **not pushed or deployed**. It supersedes the older lightweight image280effff proposal. Earlier automatic approval review rejected replacing the shared cloud API/worker without explicit owner approval; this clarification of verification behavior does not supply deployment approval. No remote deployment was retried, no resources/records changed and no production action occurred.
+
+The matching APK is **241,655,826 bytes**, SHA256 **13C6AF0FC9B77ADD78D7713AE5DFA2CD74002416EF566FBF057B84E5BDAC0BAD**, and was installed/launched on tablet `f0ba474a`. App data/settings/backend configuration were preserved by replacement installation. The [limited log/process check](evidence/trajectory-verification-2026-10-09/device-startup.json) confirms the process running and zero script/parse/fatal errors in the inspected tail; `APP_READY` was not present in that tail, so no stronger startup inference is claimed. The existing backend continues its older protocol until an approved rollout; no claim of live 2 ms verification or a physical-device competitive finish is made.
+
+Remaining: explicit deployment approval, fresh rollout checks/backup, representative live tracks/cars/bridge transitions and longest recordings, actual device complete-race acceptance and sustained server latency/capacity measurements. No layout/art or extra player-facing label was introduced, so this task requires no new UI-design screenshot.
